{"name":"Waterhen Back","hex":"#2f3f53","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"waterhen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A species of bird in the genus Amaurornis of the family Rallidae.","Synonym of turbo chook."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waterhen"},{"term":"back","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["At or near the rear.","Returned or restored to a previous place or condition."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["To or in a previous condition or place.","In a direction opposite to that in which someone or something is facing or normally pointing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back"}],"entries":[{"title":"Human back","blocks":[{"text":"The human back, also called the dorsum, is the large posterior area of the human body, rising from the top of the buttocks to the back of the neck. It is the surface of the body opposite from the chest and the abdomen. The vertebral column runs the length of the back and creates a central area of recession. The breadth of the back is created by the shoulders at the top and the pelvis at the bottom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Posterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Posterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_back","wikidata":"Q133279"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Gray204.png/120px-Gray204.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Gray204.png/250px-Gray204.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Gray204.png/120px-Gray204.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","li